<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scythian Interregnum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 653–625 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Scythian Interregnum refers to the period c. 653–625 BCE when, according to ancient tradition, Scythian nomads dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> and imposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassalage</a> on Media. It delayed the consolidation of central power. It ended with the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyaxares">Cyaxares</a>, who built the Median state into a major power.</p></div>
